okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: 'g:\\ciel-Walkie claude 세션이 바쁘게 동작할때는 sse 이벤트가 주입이 실패하는경우가 많은데 확인해봐', then '코덱스에서도 유사한문제 발생' - investigate channel/SSE message injection failures when the CLI session is busy."
answer: "Confirmed: the same pipeline fails in three distinct ways, and busy sessions are exactly what trips two of them. (1) stale_unconfirmed - the message is injected and the CLI queues it behind the running turn; after 180 s (CIEL_RUNTIME_CHANNEL_WAKE_INFLIGHT_STALE_SECONDS, default 180) the runtime gives up and records failed. (2) prompt_not_submitted - the write itself reports failure (session-socket send rejected / tty write unconfirmed). (3) real loss - Claude Code can drop a queued command (transcript queue-operation remove), and those messages never become turns. A failed record is sticky in the durable status store and blocks the scan at that cursor (channel_stdin_proxy_blocked prior_submission_failed), so later messages can stall behind it."
evidence:
  workspace: "g:\\ciel-Walkie = workspace digest aae7db361c7f, live instance router-instances/9469-aae7db361c7f (port 9469); SSE receiver 'default' -> http://100.64.0.9:8787/api/notification-delivery/stream?consumer_id=aae7db361c7f.walkie-inbox-v1, event com.ciel.walkie.support.message, input_transport=auto (resolved to session_socket)."
  status_rollup: "workspaces/aae7db361c7f/runtime-input-status.jsonl (500 requests): replied 111, failed 110 (71 stale_unconfirmed + 39 prompt_not_submitted), submitted-but-unfinished 41, queued-only 238. Failures by day: prompt_not_submitted only 2026-09-13..16; stale_unconfirmed ongoing 2026-09-18 23:39 .. 2026-09-22 08:53."
  transcript_cross_check: "Claude transcript ~/.claude/projects/G--ciel-Walkie/417ef30b-1289-47a5-8921-a4d45eb93f2e.jsonl (142 MB). Of the 180 channel messages with ids 320..499: 95 became real user turns; 15 were queued then REMOVED by the CLI (never became turns; 14 of them carry failed/stale_unconfirmed); 20 never reached the transcript and carry failed/prompt_not_submitted; 50 are absent with no failure recorded (skipped/folded paths not classified)."
  busy_turn_timing: "Request 497: queued 08:50:06, submitted 08:50:07, failed stale_unconfirmed 08:53:06 (179 s) while the transcript shows its queue-operation+user record at the same second - the turn itself was already running. Router log shows the same turn shape: POST /v1/messages tokens=982480 bytes=4039268 timeout=300.0 - this session's turns are ~1M-token, multi-minute requests, so a 180 s confirm window is routinely exceeded."
  removal_pattern: "For the 15 dropped ids the CLI wrote queue-operation operation=remove 0.1-0.3 s after a user/tool_result record; enqueue->remove deltas varied 5.7 s..495 s (no fixed TTL). Records: enqueue + attachment {type: queued_command, prompt: '[ciel-runtime external channel message] ...'} then remove; no user record follows."
  blocking: "RuntimeInputStatusRepository (runtime_input_status.py) is durable and terminal states (replied/failed) are sticky (:41-48); ChannelWakeDeliveryRepository.failure_reason() reads it (channel_wake_delivery_repository.py:38-46) and inject_pending_channel_messages() logs channel_stdin_proxy_blocked ... prior_submission_failed and returns the previous cursor (channel_pending_injection.py:125-135). Observed repeatedly in router-instances/9481-d5b7b86b83d4/router.log on 2026-09-10 (message 10 blocked for minutes)."
  timeouts: "channel_runtime_environment.py: unseen_retry_seconds default 20 (unseen_failed), inflight_stale_seconds default 180 (stale_inflight_retry -> release_stale -> failed/stale_unconfirmed), wake claim TTL 300; Codex overrides: codex_submit_retries 4, codex_submit_delay 0.25 s. commit_cursor_on_stale=False for the console namespaces (channel_terminal_proxy.py:414,639)."
  gate: "channel_pending_poll.py:120-128 - while active_tool_call()/active_turn() the poll only logs '<ns>_deferred reason=active_turn' every 30 s (channel_windows_console_deferred, 436+388 occurrences in the two Walkie instances); session_socket messages skip that gate (channel_pending_injection.py:164) so they are injected into the CLI queue instead of waiting."
  codex: "Codex workspaces: f:\\walkie-ai-bot-sandbox\\cindy (2bbe56bbee5b) 16 requests, 1 failed prompt_not_submitted (request 12: queued 22:44:01 -> failed 22:44:34; requests 13/14 stayed 'queued' while 15/16 were delivered after the instance restarted at 23:04:25); g:\\ciel-qb-mcp 11 requests, 1 prompt_not_submitted. Codex has no session socket: the injector falls back to the console path (channel_stdin_proxy_transport_fallback reason=session_socket_transport_unavailable) and writes with submit_retries=4 and a 250 ms submit delay (channel_terminal_proxy.py, runtime_launch.py:1072,1657). Codex injections confirmed via channel_wake_completed_evidence on the rollout file."
second_pass:
  question: "User asked whether failed messages pile up and block delivery at that point."
  failure_classification: "All 110 failures cross-referenced with the transcript: 59 stale_unconfirmed and 1 prompt_not_submitted were DELIVERED LATER (the message became a real user turn - a false negative, marked failed while the turn queue held it past the 180 s window); 12 stale_unconfirmed were lost (CLI queue remove, never a turn); 38 prompt_not_submitted never reached the transcript at all (the 2026-09-13..16 era). So the dominant outcome is 'reported failed but delivered late', not a permanent block."
  block_is_rare: "channel_stdin_proxy_blocked priors_submission_failed appears only in router-instances/9481-d5b7b86b83d4/router.log (2026-09-10, message 10, repeated for minutes). In the Walkie instances the queue kept moving after failures, so the block is a reachable path, not the normal behaviour."
  current_pending: "As of 2026-09-22 09:42 local: requests 498 (09:21:12), 499 (09:22:47), 500 (09:31:23) sit at 'queued' with no submit attempt; 495/496 (08:50:06, same second as 497) also never attempted. Transcript's last channel message is 497. The session itself is alive and mid-turn (transcript records to 09:42:32)."
  cannot_confirm_block: "The instance router.log has written nothing since 2026-09-22T08:38:50 and is frozen at exactly 1,000,046 bytes. RouterFileLogger.write (runtime_logging.py:150-161) rotates by path.replace(.log.1) when size > max_bytes and swallows every exception, so once the replace fails every later line is dropped - router.log.1 still carries its old mtime, i.e. rotation never completed. So whether 498-500 are blocked behind a failed cursor or consumed/skipped by another path cannot be read from the log right now. Note workspaces/aae7db361c7f/channel-llm-cursor.json has advanced to last_id 499 - the LLM delivery path claims to have consumed them."
  live_checks: "curl http://127.0.0.1:9469/health -> 200, active_client_pids [116152], provider anthropic, model ciel-runtime-anthropic-claude-opus-5[1m]; launcher pid 116152 = 'python ciel_runtime.py cli --continue' from the 335dcd8 snapshot, claude.exe pid 11684 with --model ciel-runtime-anthropic-claude-opus-5[1m]."
third_pass_delay_measured:
  user_observation: "User saw messages delivering 10+ minutes late and asked whether they pile up in a queue before injection. Confirmed, with a correction: the queue is the runtime's injection gate, not Claude's."
  measured: "96 messages with both a queued timestamp and a transcript user record: median delay 2 s, p90 99 s, max 723 s (message 500: queued 09:31:23 -> first transcript record 09:43:25, 12.0 min). Four of 96 exceed 600 s. Ids 498 (09:21:12) and 499 (09:22:47) never produced a transcript record."
  where_the_delay_is: "For 476, 482, 494 and 500 the transcript's queue-operation enqueue and the user record are 17 ms apart, so the CLI accepts an injected message instantly - there is no CLI-side queue wait. The whole delay sits before the write, in the runtime."
  gate: "poll_pending_channel_messages returns early with '<ns>_deferred reason=active_turn' whenever services.active() is true (channel_pending_poll.py:120-128); the Windows console proxy wires active = active_tool_call() or active_turn() (channel_terminal_proxy.py:343). The injector's own active_turn exemption for session_socket messages (channel_pending_injection.py:164) is never reached while the poll gate is closed."
  active_turn_semantics: "channel_transcript.py:453-458 - a Claude turn stays active until an end_turn response or a turn_duration record; the comment states that typing a wake prompt while Claude works makes Claude queue or truncate it and the verifier retries it as unseen."
  ruled_out: "channel_turn_record_exceeds_memory_limit (oversized-record skipping that could hide an end_turn) appears 0 times in 9469/9495/9481 router logs."
  still_unknown: "Why 498/499 produced no transcript record while 500 did (both same-thread supersede rules and the dead router log are candidates); the router.log has been frozen since 08:38:50 so the injector's own lines for this window do not exist."
bob_machine_unreachable:
  user_report: "'bob도 메시지를 알림을 못받고잇어' with the ssh line 'ssh -i %USERPROFILE%\\.ssh\\aap_bob -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new bob@100.64.0.6'."
  attempts: "ssh 100.64.0.6:22 and :1004 -> 'kex_exchange_identification: read: Connection reset by peer' (ssh -v: local 'SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_10.0' sent, peer reset before any server banner). Test-NetConnection: TcpTestSucceeded=True on both ports, PingSucceeded=False."
  peer_lookup: "tailscale status lists no host at 100.64.0.6 and no 'bob'/'aap-pool-bob' peer (other aap-pool-* peers are offline 7+ days); 'tailscale ping 100.64.0.6' -> 'no matching peer'. The 100.64.0.x hosts are reached over the LAN (netstat shows 10.0.0.146 -> 100.64.0.9:8787 TIME_WAIT entries), and 100.64.0.9:8787 answers 401 to an unregistered consumer_id."
    middlebox_signature: "Second pass: Test-NetConnection reports TcpTestSucceeded=True for ports 65001, 51234 and 80 on 100.64.0.6 as well, and HTTP to 100.64.0.6:8787 returns code=000 after a 3.5 ms connect - the 'open port' result is an intermediary completing handshakes, not bob. Control host 100.64.0.9 in the same /10 answers properly (8787 -> HTTP 200 in 4 ms; /api/health -> {\"status\":\"ok\",\"version\":\"0.4.2\"}, the Ciel Walkie app). So the notification source itself is healthy and reachable; only .6 (bob) is dead on this path."
outcome: "Bob's state could not be inspected from this machine; the user must supply another route (different address/port or jump host) or run the diagnostics on bob."
inferred_not_confirmed:
  - "Why Claude Code removes a queued command is not established from the logs - only that the remove lands right after a user/tool_result record. Claude Code's queue policy is not visible from outside."
  - "Whether the 50 'absent, no failure' messages were folded into an LLM-delivery request (channel_llm_inject_skipped reason=already_in_request), superseded, or skipped is not classified."
  - "No Codex busy-turn failure was reproduced in this pass (its log window for the 22:44 failure had rotated); the Codex evidence is the status file plus the shared code path."
not_done:
  - "No fix proposed or applied (user asked to check)."
  - "No live reproduction: the injector cannot be exercised without touching the live sessions."
